# Extra wallpaper directories — one directory per line, either form works:
#   ~/Pictures/Wallpapers            (tilde expands to your home)
#   /home/user/Pictures/Wallpapers   (absolute)
#   /mnt/Photos/wallpapers           (other mounts, NFS, etc.)
#
# Each directory is merged into the active theme's backgrounds as read-only
# symlinks (zz-user-<dirname>-<name>), so Noctalia's picker shows them beside
# the theme's shipped wallpapers. Your files are never copied or deleted —
# only linked. Lines starting with ~/ expand to $HOME; # comments and blank
# lines are ignored. Removing a directory prunes its links on the next refresh.
#
# Examples (uncomment to use):
# ~/Pictures/Wallpapers
# /mnt/Photos/wallpapers